# 10. Hardcoded port

## Issue

The application listens on a hardcoded port:

```js
app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});
```

This can cause deployment problems and makes it harder to run safely in containerized/cloud environments.

## Recommendation

Use an environment variable with a safe default:

```js
const port = Number(process.env.PORT) || 3000;

app.listen(port, () => {
  console.log(`Server running on port ${port}`);
});
```

