# 11. App starts listening when imported

## Issue

The file both exports `app` and starts the server:

```js
app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});

module.exports = app;
```

This can cause tests or other modules that import `app.js` to unintentionally start a server.

## Recommendation

Only start the server when this file is executed directly:

```js
if (require.main === module) {
  const port = Number(process.env.PORT) || 3000;

  app.listen(port, () => {
    console.log(`Server running on port ${port}`);
  });
}

module.exports = app;
```

