AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID,xxxx...xxxx
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY,xxxx...xxxx
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,xxxx...xxxx
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY,xxxx...xxxx
LOGFIRE_TOKEN,xxxx...xxxx
```

## Safer alternative: use fingerprints instead of first/last characters

For rotation tracking, a truncated SHA-256 fingerprint is usually safer than exposing key prefixes/suffixes.

Example:

```js
const fs = require('fs');
const crypto = require('crypto');

const envFile = process.argv[2] || '.env.test';
const contents = fs.readFileSync(envFile, 'utf8');

function fingerprint(value) {
  return crypto
    .createHash('sha256')
    .update(value)
    .digest('hex')
    .slice(0, 16);
}

for (const line of contents.split(/\r?\n/)) {
  const trimmed = line.trim();

  if (!trimmed || trimmed.startsWith('#')) continue;

  const idx = trimmed.indexOf('=');
  if (idx === -1) continue;

  const name = trimmed.slice(0, idx);
  const value = trimmed.slice(idx + 1);

  console.log(`${name},sha256:${fingerprint(value)}`);
}
```

This gives you stable tracking identifiers without revealing any part of the actual secrets.

